{"requests": [
 {"kind": "fits", "text": "ok so our infra team stood up an MCP server on Cloud Run that exposes like 40 tools (jira, confluence search, some internal billing lookups). I want my ADK agent to use maybe 6 of them, not all 40, the model gets confused. Should I use MCPToolset with SSE or streamable HTTP? Also the server sometimes takes 30+ sec on the billing calls and my agent just hangs. How do I set a sane timeout and filter the tool list? Need this working before Thursday's demo."},
 {"kind": "fits", "text": "We have a claims-triage agent built with ADK running on Agent Engine. Two other teams (fraud and customer comms) want to call it from their own agents, one of which isn't even Python/ADK. I'm thinking A2A but not sure how to expose it properly, what the agent card should advertise, how auth works across projects, and how we handle versioning when we change the input schema next quarter without breaking them. Can you walk me through the setup and review what I have in agent.py?"},
 {"kind": "elsewhere", "text": "my ADK agent has a tool that calls our internal pricing REST API and it keeps returning 403 when deployed to Cloud Run but works locally with my gcloud creds. the service account has roles/run.invoker on the pricing service. what am I missing??", "needs_instead": "This is an IAM/authentication debugging problem: getting the Cloud Run service account to mint and attach an ID token (or fixing the audience/roles) for a plain REST call. It is not about choosing or wiring an agent-to-tool-server or agent-to-agent protocol."}
]}
